WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.440
The boy who possesses Solar Hands, Azuma Kazuma,

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.690
is now employed at the Southern Tokyo Branch of the number one bakery in Japan.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.900
Together with his co-worker Kawachi Kyousuke,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.040
he has dedicated himself to the road
of making bread that lies ahead.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.280
Then, along came...

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.040
the time for Pantasia´s customary newcomers’ battle.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.160
Kazuma and Kawachi, who were both participating,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.210
had to come up with an idea for
the theme of preparing bread

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.500
on which mold would not grow.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.500
Can you really make bread like that?

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.090
Yeah, you can...

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.300
It’s <i>Japan</i> #32!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.560
I’m going to search for
<i>Japan</i> #32’s ingredients.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.810
I’ll get Kawachi’s share, as well...

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.640
Do you want Solar Hands?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.100
I know of a way...

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.900
of attaining Solar Hands...

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:56.990
10km...

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.240
I’m sure... I’m sure that it’s there.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.620
The signpost towards Solar Hands...

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.840
hidden somewhere in this swimming exercise.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.960
Definitely.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.380
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.300
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.550
In that case,
there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.910
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:24.230
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.820
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:45.080
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:53.050
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:02:00.930
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:08.640
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:16.110
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:25.490
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:34.250
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.510
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.470
is the light of only you.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.250
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:50.060
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:57.780
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.540
I won’t lose!!

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.420
I challenge you with my Osaka bread!

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.520
What the hell is this?!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.390
That’s the latest EMS model.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.140
Tsukino!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:31.020
EMS is a type of equipment which passes
currents through you to help tone your muscles.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:35.190
So, we can reinforce your muscles,
even while you’re resting.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.080
Wait up!
That’s not what I wanted to know.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.500
The sudden exercise seems to have
fatigued your muscles, hasn’t it?

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.240
There seems to be a lot of lactic acid buildup there.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.950
That’s the spirit.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.590
Come on, drink up.
This is for further reinforcement.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.430
Here you go...

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.720
What is this?

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.430
Egg white?

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.900
Egg white, being high in protein...

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.980
is perfect for building up muscles.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.480
She’s going to kill me!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.610
From now onwards...

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.240
every morning and afternoon, and before going to bed,

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.120
make sure to drink this please, okay?

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:20.860
If not...

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.360
I’ll not forgive you, all right?

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:27.830
Just a minute.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.290
What in the world is it that you’re
trying to do with the swimming?

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.000
I just want Solar Hands.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.370
I don’t really want muscle at all.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.010
Explain yourself properly!

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.380
It can’t be helped, can it?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.240
What?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.770
You want me to build up like...

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:48.690
No...

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.390
You’re telling me to become like the manager?

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.390
You don’t want that, do you?

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.020
I don’t want that!

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.900
I don’t want a body so far removed
from a human being!

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:01.200
I thought you’d say that,
and that’s why...

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.400
I avoided explaining it clearly before.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.910
Because it would have been troublesome
if you refused the training.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.040
By increasing muscle mass
all over the body,

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.710
and increasing the basic rate
of metabolism,

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.340
it’s possible to increase your body temperature...

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:16.050
Moreover, if you strengthen the muscles in your arms...

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.890
you can attain Solar Gauntlets.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.430
I definitely understand the logic.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:22.970
But...

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:24.050
This is absurd!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.480
The time for the presentation of the task for the
preliminary competition will be in one week!

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.850
It’s absurd to be doing this now.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.810
In addition, I’m still without any idea
whatsoever on how to pass it.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:37.820
Also, even if I were able to make dinner
bread that won’t grow mold,

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.320
and passed the preliminaries...

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.320
right?

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.320
How am I supposed to become all
macho in such a short period?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.580
Isn’t it obviously impossible?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.880
Then, you’re giving up on the main store, right?

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.830
I don’t really care either way.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.760
In the main store, in addition to Suwabara-san from the earlier exam,

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:02.810
people more skilled than Azuma will probably appear...

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.220
When compared to such artisans...

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:10.220
do you have the confidence to win
without even the Solar Gauntlets?

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.640
Have I been able to make you understand?

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:22.080
Either way, you have no road to take but this one.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.740
What the?

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.250
From Tokyo?!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:44.480
So, you were planning to run to Izu
in search of ingredients for your bread?

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.250
Yeah...

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.220
And halfway through, you got hungry,
lost all of your strength, and...

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.600
dropped in front of my store, did you?

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:52.230
That’s quite messed up...

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.770
But, you have quite a spirit for a kid these days...

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.900
I like that...

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.030
I’d like to give you something to eat, but...

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:07.370
Neta: topping for nigiri sushi
Nigiri sushi: hand rolled sushi/sushi ball
Since I haven’t stocked up yet, I don’t
have any toppings for nigiri sushi.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.280
Oh! There’s something good...

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.030
It’s something quick I’m rolling up, but...

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:19.000
After all, this is no good if it’s not fresh.

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.270
Here you go!
Sorry for the wait.
Makizushi: sushi rolled in nori seaweed with a core of filling. This is what he gives Kazuma.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:24.050
Makizushi: sushi rolled in nori seaweed with a core of filling. This is what he gives Kazuma.

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.020
I don’t have any money.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.980
Don’t need it. Eat up!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.860
How was that?
It’s fresh, so it’s not just spicy.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.490
The aftertaste goes away in
a steady stream, doesn’t it?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.660
However, was it a little
too much for a kid?

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.870
This is it!

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.800
This is what I wanted! This is it!

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.830
This is it!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.500
I guess it was a little too much, huh?
This is it!

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:13.130
Kawachi-kun. Leave that and handle firing the bread, will you?

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.400
Don’t touch me, you mushroom head!

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.480
Mushroom head?
That was too rude!

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:25.370
I was made to go swimming in the morning.
My entire body’s muscles are aching.

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.020
Swimming?

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:30.990
I don’t quite get what’s up, but here’s my chance!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.210
I’ll give you a massage!

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.540
What part of that is a massage?

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.040
Setting that aside...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.040
That idiot Azuma hasn’t come back yet, has he?

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:50.720
It’s almost evening.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:51.760
Azuma-san!

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:54.510
I’m back!

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.430
I’ll make <i>Japan</i> #32 immediately.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.270
Where did you go to?

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:03.820
Izu is famous for producing <i>Japan</i> #32’s ingredient.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.740
So, I headed out towards Izu to get it, but...

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.270
I found it in Miura.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:09.660
Izu?!

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:10.360
Miura?

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.780
Of Kanagawa prefecture?

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.240
Yeah.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:16.660
The old man from a sushi place
in Miura gave me some...

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.790
So I didn’t need to run to Izu.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.290
Is that so? That’s good...

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.340
Is that really the point?

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:27.080
No one’s going to admonish him about
just going off like that, huh?

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.210
It’s done!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.850
This is <i>Japan</i> #32.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:35.640
That’s a really savory fragrance.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:38.060
Is this the dinner bread that won’t grow mold?

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:39.300
Yeah.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.070
Come on, eat up!

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.070
I’m going to pass.

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:45.810
Huh?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:50.810
Either way, with my body like this,
I won’t be able to stand any reactions.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.160
Kawachi-san...

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.330
If <i>Japan</i> #32 turns out really delicious,

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.780
I won’t be able to use the same ingredients to win.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:03.260
What’s up with him?

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.920
Please don’t worry about it.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.260
I’ll partake without any reservations.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:09.750
Me, too!

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.980
A strong breeze is blowing through my nose.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:26.490
Serene spring waters overflow from beneath my eyelids.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:30.020
So still...

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.450
Into rocks it pierces...

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.040
The shrillness of cicadas...

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.910
This is truly Matsuo Bashou’s world of wabi and sabi.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.540
No, this is the world of wasabi!

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.660
Ah! I’m not at all sad.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.630
I’m actually really happy.
But tears are flowing.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.680
Because I’m a girl after all...

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.750
Tsukino-san has really changed.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:53.840
This spiciness is...

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:54.760
wasabi?

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:55.750
That’s right!

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.540
This is my wasabi dinner bread.
<i>Japan</i> #32!

00:10:58.540 --> 00:10:59.600
Wasabi, he says!

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:04.480
But, the wasabi-sushi rolls I ate
at Miura were really good...

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.980
But I think that if it’s wasabi,

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.310
you could buy it at the neighborhood
supermarket as well, though...

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:09.730
Is that so?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.730
Wasabi, huh?

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.280
Manager!

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:13.320
I see...

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:17.070
The allyl-mustard oil present in wasabi

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.910
has strong antimicrobial properties,

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:23.450
and has been scientifically shown
to prevent bacterial growth.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.830
Therefore, it can also prevent the growth of mold.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.330
H-However, can wasabi and bread
complement each other?

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:32.510
Since olden times, in the West,

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:34.750
if was customary to put the source of the
reputed wasabi, horseradish, into bread.

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.750
Wasabi and bread complement each other perfectly.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.760
I’ve been rolled over again.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.020
You were amazing, Azuma-san.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:50.680
Hmm. It’s delicious.
I could really get used to this taste.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.150
Right? Right?

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.190
Eat more!

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.940
It might be impossible for me.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.740
Even if I didn’t make it
to the main store,

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.160
and I were to continue working here quietly...

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:05.120
I’d be able to improve my skills
to those of a decent baker.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.300
I’d be able to save up money, bit by bit.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.040
I’m sorry, everyone.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.710
The main store was set

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:15.310
on a much steeper hill than your brother could handle.

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:20.170
What?

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.420
You loser...

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.890
What the hell are you doing, you idiot?

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.060
What?

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:30.980
I was just drowning the sorrows of
the cowardly loser that you are.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:31.940
What did you say?

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.350
Manager!

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:34.480
Kawachi!

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.480
You’re annoying. Sulking like that.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.580
What the hell are you doing?!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.420
This here was first-class sake.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:58.090
So good that it’s wasted on the head of a loser like you.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.590
What was that?!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:04.600
Either way, a coward like you has no
way of getting into the main store.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:08.460
Drown yourself in alcohol or whatever,
and forget about your impossible dream!

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:16.190
Kawachi!

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.240
Kawachi!

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:24.170
Manager!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.910
That was a little too cruel, saying it to him like that...

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:32.340
You had also acknowledged his passion, hadn’t you?

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:39.760
There are times when it’s good
to be cold towards a man.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.670
We’re troublesome creatures, we are...

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:44.380
Manager...

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:49.890
And what about me...? Who I think, as always, has been treated coldly...

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.740
Me, a loser?

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:01.770
He said a lot there...

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:02.960
Dammit...

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.950
Kawachi!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:15.750
Kawachi!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.880
What are you trying to do?!

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.340
Have you come here to jeer at me, too? You idiot.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.590
Huh?

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:26.680
Kawachi!

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:30.100
Don’t come here! You have it easy, don’t you? You really annoy me!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.610
Where are you hurt?

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:34.430
Huh?

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.810
Yeah, there it is!

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.360
See, the bridge of your nose is all bent.

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:41.270
This happened just now, when I fell.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:42.610
Huh?

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.990
So where else did you hurt yourself?

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:48.150
Because you were drenched in
sake by the manager, right?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:49.280
Huh?

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:53.790
When I would get hurt as a child,
my grandpa used to pour sake on me as well.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.120
It hurts, Grandpa.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:57.540
Antiseptic’s coming!

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.090
Sake jet!

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:02.710
He told me at that time,
“Antiseptic coming!”

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.250
But that really stings, doesn’t it?

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:08.760
However, after applying antiseptic, it’s a good idea to place a band-aid there, okay?

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.810
He’s... he’s an idiot.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.060
Look here...

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.350
I wasn’t sprayed with sake because
I needed an antiseptic.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.190
Huh?

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:22.280
What needs antiseptic is his brain.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:24.780
Wait. Antiseptic?

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.490
That’s not good.

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:27.990
If you don’t disinfect it,

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:30.910
the bacteria will spread all over
your body, and it’ll be terrible!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.740
Bacteria... antiseptic...

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.580
Maybe... this was what... that old man...

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.540
No!

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:40.750
I’m thinking too much.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.130
That cannot be possible.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.300
This is what I’ve thought of.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.630
This might work.
Bread that does not grow mold.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.260
If you need wasabi, there’s still some left.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.140
I don’t need something like that!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.140
I will make it my own way.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.150
Wait up, Kawachi!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.230
I’ve noticed it.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:06.150
However, I don’t think at all that
it was thanks to you, Manager.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.410
I... I noticed it all on my own.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.580
Ah! Kawachi-san.

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:15.620
Where’s the manager?

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.580
He said that he was,going to go do some shopping...

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.410
That’s good then.
Do you have a band-aid?

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.830
Huh? Yeah... probably...

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.710
Miss... it looks like I’ll be able to make it, too.

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:29.300
Bread on which it’s difficult for mold to grow.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:32.340
Huh? Without using wasabi?

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.550
Of course!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.470
Don’t be underestimating Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:35.530
That’s not good.
It’s not fermented enough.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:36.870
Dammit.

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:38.330
This isn’t going to work then?

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.750
No, it has come up to quite a decent stage.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:43.580
Just a little more...

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:50.590
It can’t be helped.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:53.810
We’ll let the special training pass for today.

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:05.850
All right!

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:07.560
My first-born!

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:10.110
Morning!

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:12.660
Ah. Morning!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.860
Again with the rude language.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.740
Normally, to a senior such as myself,
shouldn’t it be “Good morning?”

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.120
God, this year’s newcomers...

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:22.500
Anyone, and everyone...

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.170
Hmm? This smell...

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.080
It’s done!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.260
This is Kawachi-style dinner bread.

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:40.000
Is this the bread on which it’s
difficult for mold to grow?

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.470
Are you done with it, Kawachi?

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.480
Of course. Who do you think I am?

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.400
This really gives off a nice smell...

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.860
Yeah, doesn’t it?
Let’s sample it right off.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.690
Please wait just one moment.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:54.610
What?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.570
I understand about the newcomers’ battle, but...

00:18:56.570 --> 00:19:00.490
Can we not have you turn your attention
towards the store a little more?

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:05.040
Try putting yourself in my shoes, always
being the only one working seriously.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:09.840
Got it. In thanks for your hard work,
I’ll let you sample it first.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:11.470
Here.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.040
Looks good, doesn’t it?

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.460
Aren’t you going to eat it?

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:19.350
My hard work is not so cheap as to
be brushed off with just this, okay?

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.690
Man, always. Always.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:31.390
This is... really... delicious...

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:36.950
Moreover, who do you guys think you are?

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.610
I should just quit. This kind of store...

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:47.620
That’d teach you how hard it’d be without me.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.630
He appears to be drunk, doesn’t he?

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:52.040
The fool!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.140
The Manager has an algae-like head.

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:56.840
Don’t tell me...

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.630
Kawachi-san, did you add sake to the bread?

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.180
That’s right.

00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:04.510
I added plenty of brandy to the
dough, and then baked it.

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:08.640
This is my sake-bread, soon to become <i>Osaka-pan</i> #1!

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:12.360
Your sake-bread, becoming <i>Osaka-pan</i> #1?

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.200
O-baka Man #1?

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.690
Yet another pun, is it?

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.710
Anyone, and everyone...

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:26.450
Alcohol, like wasabi, possesses
strong antimicrobial properties.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.210
It’s used in western confectionery, right?

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:31.340
So I thought that it might go well with bread also...

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:33.040
That’s pretty good, Kawachi!

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:35.580
You don’t need to say that.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.090
Could it be that the manager
was trying to...?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.840
Who is it?!

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:45.140
Who was thoughtless enough to make him drink sake?

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:45.890
Flap and flutter.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:46.560
This guy goes crazy from just
Flap and flutter.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.650
This guy goes crazy from just

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.940
sniffing alcohol fumes.

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:54.440
Manager.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:58.440
What?

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:01.100
I would’ve thought that a certain gutless
somebody must’ve missed his mother’s

00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:03.400
breasts enough to have gone back to the country.

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.990
Manager!

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:07.200
No, Kawachi-san!

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.630
Thank you very much!

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:27.980
Kawachi-san.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.060
Kawachi.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:43.910
It’s the first time I’ve been thanked
by someone I threw sake on.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.030
You’re really something...

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:57.790
Manager, where are you going?

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.540
I have to replenish my energy source.

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:05.050
I ended up doing something so wasteful as to share it...

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:07.810
with a certain someone.

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:16.350
Hey!

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:21.110
What’s with drinking so early in the morning?

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:24.450
He really is the O-baka Man.

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:46.680
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:55.690
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:22:59.260 --> 00:23:06.700
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:11.870
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:18.010
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:18.010 --> 00:23:20.580
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:20.810 --> 00:23:24.720
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:29.490
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:33.330
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:38.030
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:43.200
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:43.470 --> 00:23:52.010
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:52.410 --> 00:24:01.370
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:06.060 --> 00:24:07.440
The newcomers’ battle.

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:09.020
Let’s do if together, shall we, Kawachi?

00:24:09.020 --> 00:24:09.560
Idiot.

00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:11.190
We’re rivals.

00:24:11.190 --> 00:24:12.650
Don’t talk to me so easily.

00:24:12.650 --> 00:24:13.730
Oh, my.

00:24:13.730 --> 00:24:14.930
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:18.450
Each one’s opening curtain!!
The Pantasia newcomers’ battle begins!

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:20.020
Watch it, okay?

00:24:20.490 --> 00:24:22.770
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.660
Leftover delicious bread can be preserved in the freezer.

00:24:25.660 --> 00:24:26.910
Fr-ee-zer.

00:24:26.910 --> 00:24:29.540
The temperature of the fridge does
not prevent aging of the starch,

00:24:29.540 --> 00:24:31.750
which leads to a loss of taste!

00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:33.180
Heh?!
